<article class="env-proposition" id="FBFAD3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FBFAD3">Proposition <span data-tag="FBFAD3">6.5.2.1</span> <span class="named">(Jardine <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/jardine">jardine</a>]</span>)</span>.</a>model category!local There exists a left proper, combinatorial, simplicial model structure on the category $\mathbf{A}$, which admits the following description: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(C)$"><p>
A map $f: F_{\bullet } \rightarrow G_{\bullet }$ of simplicial presheaves on $\calC $ is a <em>local cofibration</em> if it is a injective cofibration: that is, if and only if the induced map $F_{\bullet }(C) \rightarrow G_{\bullet }(C)$ is a cofibration of simplicial sets for each object $C \in \calC $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(W)$"><p>
A map $f: F_{\bullet } \rightarrow G_{\bullet }$ of simplicial presheaves on $\calC $ is a <em>local equivalence</em> if and only if, for any object $C \in \calC $ and any commutative diagram of topological spaces 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { S^{n-1} \ar [r] \ar @{^{(}->}[d] &amp;  |F_{\bullet }(C)| \ar [d] \\ D^ n \ar [r] &amp;  |G_{\bullet }(C)|, }  \]
</div>
<p>
 there exists a collection of morphisms $\{  C_{\alpha } \rightarrow C\} $ which generate a covering sieve on $C$, such that in each of the induced diagrams 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { S^{n-1} \ar [r] \ar @{^{(}->}[d] &amp;  |F_{\bullet }(C_{\alpha })| \ar [d] \\ D^ n \ar [r] \ar @{-->}[ur] &amp;  |G_{\bullet }(C_{\alpha })|, }  \]
</div>
<p>
 one can produce a dotted arrow so that the upper triangle commutes and the lower triangle commutes up to a homotopy which is fixed on $S^{n-1}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>